{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-253241" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that\n$D=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}],$\nfind $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi D}{6}).$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi D}{6})=\\,\\,$ |  | $0$ | {{field-4}} | {{field-5}} |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | $0$ | {{field-6}} |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072904/state.json" "file_sha256" "76111f53c72140f59c241c3f717c2a7d4fe7e3279c7037bd23160a68ed3ffea3"} {"question" "q-253241" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given a function $f$ and a diagonal matrix $D$ with diagonal entries ${\\lambda }_{1},…,{\\lambda }_{n},$ we have\n\n$$\nf(D)=[\\begin{aligned}f({\\lambda }_{1}) & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & f({\\lambda }_{n})\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi D}{6}) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{6}) & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{6}) & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{6})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072904/state.json" "file_sha256" "76111f53c72140f59c241c3f717c2a7d4fe7e3279c7037bd23160a68ed3ffea3"} {"question" "q-253241" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072904/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4ea4643011baa08ce614f164a25cebc94985e23735a38af1c21837f9d01af7d1"} {"question" "q-253241" "fie