{{field-3}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\sqrt{{J}_{3}(4)}=\\,\\,$ |  | $0$ | {{field-4}} | {{field-5}} |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | $0$ | {{field-6}} |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072904/state.json" "file_sha256" "76111f53c72140f59c241c3f717c2a7d4fe7e3279c7037bd23160a68ed3ffea3"} {"question" "q-253421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given a function $f$ and a Jordan block ${J}_{n}(\\lambda ),$ we have\n\n$$\nf({J}_{n}(\\lambda ))=[\\begin{aligned}f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) & \\frac{{f}^{″}(\\lambda )}{2!} & ⋯ & \\frac{{f}^{(n-1)}(\\lambda )}{(n-1)!} \\\\ 0 & f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) & ⋯ & \\frac{{f}^{(n-2)}(\\lambda )}{(n-2)!} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋱ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & 0 & f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & ⋯ & 0 & f(\\lambda )\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $f(x)=\\sqrt{x},$ $n=3,$ and $\\lambda =4.$\n\nSince $n=3,$ we need to compute the first $3-1=2$ derivatives of $f:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\sqrt{x}={x}^{1/2} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{-3/2}=-\\frac{1}{4x\\sqrt{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({J}_{3}(2)) & =[\\begin{aligned}f(4) & {f}^{′}(4) & \\frac{{f}^{″}(4)}{2!} \\\\ 0 & f(4) & {f}^{′}(4) \\\\ 0 & 0 & f(4)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{4} & \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{4}} & -\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 4\\cdot 4\\sqrt{4}} \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{4} & \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{4}} \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\sqrt{4}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & \\frac{1}{4} & -\\frac{1}{64} \\\\ 0 & 2 & \\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072904/state.json" "file_sha256" "76111f53c72140f59c241c3f717c2a7d4fe7e3279c7037bd23160a68ed3ffea3"} {"question" "q